{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgaLBZfEkSG2N95zmyk8c","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I implemented `parse_duration` in `duration.py`, and it passes every example in TASK.md plus about 30 edge cases I checked by hand (Python 3.9.6, standard library only).\n\nThe approach:\n- **Validation** uses anchored regexes, so only the grammar's forms are accepted. `[0-9]` is used instead of `\\d` so non-ASCII digits are rejected.\n- **Unit form** sums parts with `fractions.Fraction`, so `0.1h` gives exactly 360 and `0.3s` is rejected as a non-whole result. Units must be strictly decreasing, which also rejects repeats.\n- **Clock form** uses a Horner-style fold over the fields, so `M:SS` and `H:MM:SS` share one path.\n- **Sign and whitespace** are handled by stripping the input, then removing one leading `-`.\n- **Non-`str` input** raises `TypeError`, and every other invalid input raises `ValueError`.\n\nDecision for you: I read \"the bare string `0`\" literally, so `-0` is rejected, while `-0s` returns 0. If you want `-0` accepted as a bare zero, that is a one-line change.\n\nI tested with an inline script run under `python3 -I` rather than adding a test file, so the project directory only contains the edited `duration.py`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4881,"cache_read_input_tokens":26051,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4881},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4e788472-a1b5-4fbb-82e7-887cf8a34627","uuid":"6349bbdc-4660-4bf1-9310-649452b9e1ae","timestamp":"2026-10-31T12:41:05.357Z","request_id":"req_011CgaLBZHRhCVNXSc5Usmqb"}
